Part 5: Making Permanent Changes
Safety Design
All changes initially occur in a test copy of your network. The original network remains unchanged until explicitly updated.
Applying Changes
1. Modify All
•	Available for Above, Below, and Closest to conditions
•	Modifies all elements matching the condition
•	Displays a warning before applying changes
Example: Modify all pipes with diameter above 0.3 m.
2. Update Original Network
•	Final step after completing testing and analysis
•	Copies all test modifications to the original network
•	Requires confirmation
Reset Modifications
•	Reverts all changes made during the session
•	Restores the test network to its original state
